;; meta-signal-mentci — the META policy / authority signal for the mentci
;; programmable-UI daemon (Spirit 7sx6: signal-<c> + meta-signal-<c> are the
;; TWO contracts; Signal / Nexus / SEMA are the runtime engines inside the
;; daemon). This is the second of mentci's two contracts; the ordinary working
;; wire is signal-mentci (already built + validated). Wire-only: schema-emitted
;; rkyv plus the optional NOTA codec on the signal-frame request/reply envelope.
;; No daemon, actor runtime, transport, database, or rendering implementation —
;; those live in the mentci daemon (mentci-egui / mentci-lib) and its thin
;; clients. SELF-CONTAINED VOCABULARY.
;;
;; Charter (mirrors meta-signal-criome): meta-only authority / configuration.
;; Ordinary programmable-UI traffic — present a question, push an update,
;; observe state, answer — stays in signal-mentci. Daemon startup and meta
;; reconfiguration live HERE. The two share one component identity but two
;; contracts: the working signal carries traffic, the meta signal carries the
;; policy that configures who the daemon trusts and how it surfaces itself.
;;
;; The single meta verb is Configure, exactly mirroring meta-signal-criome:
;;   (Configure MentciDaemonConfiguration)
;;     -> Configured | ConfigurationRejected | RequestUnimplemented
;;
;; MentciDaemonConfiguration carries the daemon's startup + reconfiguration
;; policy (Spirit 7x5z — the state-bearing programmable-UI daemon):
;;   component_sockets     — typed component connection-points by authority lane
;;   persona_identity      — the persona Identity that is the signing principal
;;   notification_clients  — which notification surfaces are enabled
;;
;; DAEMON-CONFIG-IS-BINARY (component override): a daemon accepts only a
;; pre-generated rkyv startup/meta message — never inline NOTA, never a .nota
;; path. This contract is that binary message's TYPE. A virgin daemon may start
;; unconfigured and wait for an authenticated binary meta-signal Configure
;; before it serves; on restart it self-resumes from persisted SEMA state.
;;
;; CROSS-IMPORT DEFERRED (Woe 4 / 681). Two types would ideally import from
;; signal-standard: ComponentKind (the closed component roster) and the eaf7
;; typed connection-point (StandardSocket). signal-standard is NOT YET A CRATE,
;; so this contract declares its own local equivalents, each tagged with its
;; eventual cross-import source. signal-criome is also still on the stale
;; dot-field notation (Woe 4) and will not lower under current main's positional
;; grammar, so the criome-facing socket is the local StandardSocket too — no
;; signal-criome cross-import is attempted. Local types marked
;;   ;; (cross-import target: signal-standard:lib:…)
;; identify the eventual import source. When signal-standard lands, the local
;; ComponentKind / StandardSocket declarations collapse into an import brace
;;   { ComponentKind signal-standard:lib:ComponentKind
;;     StandardSocket signal-standard:lib:StandardSocket }
;; with no other change to the verb roster or the configuration shape.
;;
;; GRAMMAR NOTE (current schema main, b3be7d0 — past abae95f). The
;; positional struct-field grammar uses explicit field roles: a field with a
;; name that differs from its type is written field.Type (dot form) only when
;; the same payload type appears more than once in the product. A field whose
;; type is unique in the product is written as the bare type (derived name) —
;; writing field.Type there is an ExplicitFieldOnUniqueProductComponent error;
;; a collection field carries its role as a dot-bound field name,
;; FieldRole.(Vector Element), whose snake-case becomes the field name. The
;; retired two-atom  field Type  pair no longer lowers. A single-field brace
;; collapses to a NEWTYPE over its one reference and must use the bare payload
;; type, so StandardSocket, Configured, and ConfigurationRejected lower as
;; newtypes carrying exactly the one-field payload — multi-field braces
;; (PersonaIdentity, MentciDaemonConfiguration, RequestUnimplemented) stay
;; structs.

;; -------------------------------------------------------------------
;; Input root — the one meta verb. Mirrors meta-signal-criome exactly.
;; -------------------------------------------------------------------
[(Configure MentciDaemonConfiguration)]

;; -------------------------------------------------------------------
;; Output root — the three meta replies. Mirrors meta-signal-criome
;; exactly: a generation receipt, a typed rejection, an unimplemented
;; sentinel for verbs not yet wired.
;; -------------------------------------------------------------------
[(Configured Configured)
 (ConfigurationRejected ConfigurationRejected)
 (RequestUnimplemented RequestUnimplemented)]

{
  ;; -------------------------------------------------------------------
  ;; Primitive newtypes. Distinct newtypes, not transparent aliases
  ;; (Spirit qz6j: aliases offer no correctness and are not used).
  ;; -------------------------------------------------------------------
  SocketPath Path
  PersonaName String
  PersonaKeyLabel String
  ConfigurationGeneration Integer

  ;; -------------------------------------------------------------------
  ;; StandardSocket — the eaf7 typed connection-point. A typed Unix-socket
  ;; path is the local case; the network host+port case is the off-box
  ;; extension, deliberately not modeled in this single-machine UI-daemon
  ;; slice (Q3 confirms single-machine scope). It is always wrapped in a
  ;; ComponentSocket so every path carries the component and authority lane it
  ;; reaches.
  ;; (cross-import target: signal-standard:lib:StandardSocket — the standard
  ;;  connection-point type; deferred while signal-standard is not yet a
  ;;  crate. signal-criome's own socket is NOT cross-imported either: that
  ;;  contract is still on stale dot-field notation, Woe 4.)
  ;; -------------------------------------------------------------------
  StandardSocket {
    SocketPath
  }

  ;; -------------------------------------------------------------------
  ;; ComponentSocket — one typed connection-point for a component authority
  ;; lane. Mentci can connect to multiple components, so socket paths are not
  ;; positional "ordinary/meta" fields. The kind names both the component and
  ;; whether the socket is its working or meta-policy channel.
  ;; -------------------------------------------------------------------
  ComponentSocketKind [
    Mentci
    MetaMentci
    Criome
    MetaCriome
    Introspect
    MetaIntrospect
  ]
  ComponentSocket {
    ComponentSocketKind
    StandardSocket
  }

  ;; -------------------------------------------------------------------
  ;; ComponentKind — the closed component roster (681 reconciliation, 14
  ;; variants across five documented zones). Declared local here PENDING the
  ;; signal-standard crate; the persona Identity below names which component
  ;; the signing principal speaks for, and the criome socket below names a
  ;; Criome peer. Carried in full so the local declaration is faithful to the
  ;; eventual import and nothing is silently narrowed.
  ;; (cross-import target: signal-standard:lib:ComponentKind — the closed,
  ;;  zone-partitioned roster; deferred while signal-standard is not yet a
  ;;  crate. Persona is a principal, not a daemon — see 681 § 2.)
  ;; -------------------------------------------------------------------
  ComponentKind [
    Spirit
    Mind
    Criome
    Message
    Router
    Mirror
    Terminal
    Harness
    Agent
    System
    Introspect
    Orchestrate
    Lojix
    Persona
  ]

  ;; -------------------------------------------------------------------
  ;; PersonaIdentity — the signing principal. The persona Identity whose
  ;; sub-key signs the psyche verdict that mentci escalates to criome. Names
  ;; the persona, the component it speaks for (normally Persona), and the
  ;; key label criome decrypts at login (q1le — the encrypted multi-key
  ;; store; the daemon never holds the raw key, criome custodies it).
  ;; -------------------------------------------------------------------
  PersonaIdentity {
    PersonaName
    ComponentKind
    PersonaKeyLabel
  }

  ;; -------------------------------------------------------------------
  ;; NotificationClient — a surface the daemon may push notifications to.
  ;; The thin-client surfaces from 7x5z: a status bar, a popup, an email
  ;; egress. Enabling a client here turns its push path on; the canonical
  ;; InterfaceState (signal-mentci) is what actually fans out to it.
  ;; -------------------------------------------------------------------
  NotificationClient [
    StatusBar
    Popup
    Email
  ]

  ;; -------------------------------------------------------------------
  ;; MentciDaemonConfiguration — the daemon startup + reconfiguration
  ;; message. THIS is the binary rkyv blob a deploy/bootstrap tool encodes
  ;; and hands the daemon (component override: daemons never parse NOTA,
  ;; configuration included). Carries: typed component sockets, the persona
  ;; signing principal, and which notification surfaces are enabled.
  ;; -------------------------------------------------------------------
  MentciDaemonConfiguration {
    ComponentSockets.(Vector ComponentSocket)
    PersonaIdentity
    NotificationClients.(Vector NotificationClient)
  }

  ;; -------------------------------------------------------------------
  ;; Reply payloads. Mirror meta-signal-criome exactly.
  ;; -------------------------------------------------------------------

  ;; Configured — the configuration was applied; the generation counter
  ;; advances so the caller can confirm which configuration is live. A plain
  ;; monotonic counter (Q3: a single-machine UI daemon needs no AttestedMoment
  ;; on a local config-generation counter — designer recommendation).
  Configured {
    ConfigurationGeneration
  }

  ConfigurationRejectionReason [
    ManagerAuthorityRequired
    MalformedConfiguration
    StoreUnavailable
  ]
  ConfigurationRejected {
    ConfigurationRejectionReason
  }

  ;; RequestUnimplemented — the sentinel for a meta verb that is declared but
  ;; not yet wired in this daemon build. OperationKind is the single-verb
  ;; roster mirroring meta-signal-criome (Configure only); UnimplementedReason
  ;; distinguishes not-built-yet from a missing dependency.
  OperationKind [Configure]
  UnimplementedReason [NotBuiltYet DependencyNotReady]
  RequestUnimplemented {
    OperationKind
    UnimplementedReason
  }
}
